{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtMyN9ACe7BeqypWQ88U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`, which runs the same Codex call as the `codex` lane inside `sandbox/agent.sb`. The lane can't run here yet, because it needs `CODEX_API_KEY` and this machine doesn't have one set. It exits 2 with a message until you set one or choose another auth route.\n\n**The problem:** Codex's `-o` file can't be written inside the sandbox if it lands in the real home, and Codex still exits 0. This matches the colleague's note. It only bites when the run folder is under the real home, as in the README's eval-Mac layout (`~/evals/agent-evals`). The lane writes `-o` into a scratch folder in `/tmp` and copies the file into the run folder after the sandbox exits. If Codex exits 0 with no output, the lane returns exit code 3.\n\n**Auth is the open decision.** On this machine, Codex logs in with OAuth tokens in the real `~/.codex`, not an API key. The sandbox hides that folder, so the lane needs a key. I didn't take either workaround:\n- Opening `~/.codex` in `agent.sb` would also let the kimi lane's shell read Codex's tokens.\n- Copying `auth.json` into the scratch home might break the real `codex` lane, because refresh tokens can rotate. I haven't checked whether they do.\n\nYour options: set `CODEX_API_KEY` for this lane, or give codex runs their own profile that opens only `~/.codex`. I'd pick the key.\n\n**What I verified** (no model calls):\n- The sandbox denies writes under the real home and allows writes under `/tmp`. `codex --version` runs inside the profile.\n- With a stub `codex`, the output file is copied out and the real home is untouched. The no-output case returns exit 3. The missing-key guard exits 2.\n- `bash -n` passes. The test run folders are removed.\n\n**Not verified:** a real run against OpenAI. I didn't want to send the task to a provider without your go-ahead. Once a key is set, run `CODEX_API_KEY=... ./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1`.\n\n**Changes:** `run.sh` (new lane, header comment, dispatch line), `README.md` (lane description), and `ANSWER.md` (the write-up, including which parts of the colleague's note applied). `agent.sb` and the kimi lane are unchanged. I did not commit.\n\n**Also flagged:** the README says Codex \"needs nothing from the home folder.\" That's not true on this machine, where the existing `codex` lane depends on `~/.codex`. I left the sentence as it was, so please check it against the eval Mac."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_read_input_tokens":54967,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1483},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df6ac1de-6d70-4cc0-b851-936c6e620114","uuid":"be15752a-2ac6-49ff-94c5-8c2a5ded37dc","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:15:17.296Z","request_id":"req_011CgtMyMxW13ZuURabAtiaf"}
